{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "What Happened Last Night?", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Stressful Night", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 13, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange information about hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le13ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Stress with Suffixes: Three Syllable on the Suffix ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You stress words differently according to their <span class=\"strong\">suffix patterns</span>. The syllable stressed in the word will depend on the <span class=\"strong\">suffix pattern</span> that the word follows.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Words ending in -ee, -eer, and -ese are stressed on the<span class=\"strong\"> last syllable</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the following words and pay attention to proper emphasis and suffix stress:<br/> guaran<span class=\"strong\">tee</span><br/> emplo<span class=\"strong\">yee</span><br/> over<span class=\"strong\">see</span><br/> engin<span class=\"strong\">eer</span><br/> sights<span class=\"strong\">eer</span><br/> volunt<span class=\"strong\">eer</span><br/> Japan<span class=\"strong\">ese</span><br/> Canton<span class=\"strong\">ese</span><br/> Vietnam<span class=\"strong\">ese</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "He guaran<span class=\"strong\">teed</span> the shipment would be here at 4:00 pm.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We're short-handed three employ<span class=\"strong\">ees</span>.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Are you with the Asian engineer committ<span class=\"strong\">ee</span>?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I need you to over<span class=\"strong\">see</span> the bar.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We have Japan<span class=\"strong\">ese</span>, Chin<span class=\"strong\">ese</span>, Vietnam<span class=\"strong\">ese</span>, Korean and Canton<span class=\"strong\">ese</span> from Hong Kong.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Would you like che<span class=\"strong\">ese</span> and crackers?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We have two sight<span class=\"strong\">see</span>rs and I am a volun<span class=\"strong\">teer</span>.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Intonation in Non-Final Thought Groups", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A thought group refers to a coherent unit of speech that forms a whole. You normally separate a long sentence into several thought groups, held together by thematic content or by natural pauses in the sentence.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Non-final thought groups represent all the thought groups that you say before the last thought group of a sentence. The final thought group is the thought group that ends a sentence.<br/> You stress non-final thought groups differently from final thought groups.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You normally stress non-final thought groups with a normal-rising-normal pattern.<br/> You stress final thought groups with a normal-rising-falling pattern.<br/>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I'll take <span class=\"strong\">car</span>e of them, / I need you to oversee the <span class=\"strong\">bar</span>. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">just</span> called her on the <span class=\"strong\">pho</span>ne. She <span class=\"strong\">said</span> she's <span class=\"strong\">sick</span> / and <span class=\"strong\">can</span>'t come in.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Rachel told <span class=\"strong\">me</span> / they were in a car <span class=\"strong\">accident</span>.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Would you like <span class=\"strong\">Mer</span>lot / or <span class=\"strong\">Sauvignon</span>?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Would you like <span class=\"strong\">white</span> / or <span class=\"strong\">red</span>?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">My name is Vanessa, and I will be serving you this evening.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "&nbsp&nbsp\u2192&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp\u2192&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp\u2192&